1
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:07,055
Feast your eyes on that rat, would ya?

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,240
Dumb nation! Woo!

3
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:20,637
This bastard must have
died right quick, like.

4
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,720
Fell off that cliff, I'll warrant.

5
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:24,477
Courage wheels slipped in the mud.

6
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:28,442
They weren't hurting for coin, if
these fine clothes tell it true.

7
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:32,437
Dario, the lady is dead,
but the baby with her.

8
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:34,440
It's still alive, I can hear it.

9
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:38,060
She must have protected it
with her body. Leave it be.

10
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:39,929
Soon enough it'll be dead.

11
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:42,120
What are you doing?

12
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:44,660
You've got eyes, ain't you, woman?

13
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,940
I'm appropriating his jewellery, huh?

14
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:49,760
What have we here?

15
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:53,286
Evil-looking thing, ain't it?

16
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:55,677
Well, fetch me nothing.

17
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:56,720
Hey!

18
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:57,720
Lend a hand!

19
00:00:57,940 --> 00:00:59,940
Help me yank out his pearly teeth!

20
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:02,105
They'll fetch a pretty copper!

21
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:08,660
Providence sends me aid in the
guise of a man. Many thanks.

22
00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:11,977
My wife.

23
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:13,557
My wife and son.

24
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:15,420
Tell me, do they live?

25
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:21,200
I hate to say it, but your wife, Saint's
Preserver, has gone on to a heavenly rest.

26
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,020
But the baby is alive and well.

27
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:27,437
Fate is...

28
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:28,600
most cruel.

29
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:31,960
My name is George Joestar.

30
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:35,080
You have saved my life this cursed night.

31
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:40,540
Quickly tell me your name that I may
remember before my senses fail me.

32
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:45,320
This peacock thinks I'm here
out of the goodness of me heart.

33
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:48,537
Little does he know.

34
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,360
Guess I'll oblige him.

35
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:53,040
Doriel Brando, your lordship.

36
00:01:54,380 --> 00:02:00,240
Sir, I swear to you, the Joestar family
will honor the debt we have incurred.

37
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:14,520
Ah, there's a good boy.

38
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:17,480
Father, I'm off!

39
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:20,980
Then fare thee well,
Jojo. Let's go, Danny.

40
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:32,940
T .O.

41
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:36,320
Mind your father.

42
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:40,940
Damn your eyes, you
lazy boy. Are you deaf?

43
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:46,540
What do you want, father? Medicine?

44
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:47,800
You idiot.

45
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,962
Their snake oil does me no good.

46
00:02:50,180 --> 00:02:51,010
Get out of here.

47
00:02:51,093 --> 00:02:53,998
And don't come back until
you've found me some booze.

48
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:02,760
Your manners are dreadful.

49
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:04,840
Forgive me, father.

50
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:06,570
Checkmate.

51
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:11,160
Take it.

52
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:19,140
Don't feel so smart now, do you, Welp?

53
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:29,560
Oh, let me guess, Serena, your daddy
bought you this doll, didn't he?

54
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:30,930
It's fancy.

55
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:33,236
Being a quack must pay him real nice.

56
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,150
I know.

57
00:03:35,233 --> 00:03:38,037
What do you say we peel off
this fancy-looking dress, huh?

58
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:41,197
And see if they made her with all
the real girl bits underneath.

59
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,110
Me.

60
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:44,960
Oh my god!

61
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,200
Arena's a crybaby!

62
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,260
Arena's a crybaby!

63
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:50,810
Arena's a crybaby!

64
00:03:50,893 --> 00:03:51,723
That's enough!

65
00:03:51,806 --> 00:03:53,285
Give it back to her right now!

66
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,282
Who's this guy?

67
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:56,257
You some friend of Arena's?

68
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:59,634
I've never met her, but I'll
fight for her all the same!

69
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:04,660
Who is this idiot getting in a
fight for a girl he don't even know?

70
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:10,860
Looks like somebody It
was nothing but chalk.

71
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:14,677
Look at him there on the ground.

72
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:15,877
Are you going to cry?

73
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:18,901
Some knight in shining
armor you turned out to be.

74
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,430
Huh?

75
00:04:22,513 --> 00:04:24,909
This little panty waist
is the Joestar kid.

76
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:29,657
Now that I know you're some rich
guy's son, we're just getting started.

77
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:31,799
You can't buy your way out of this.

78
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:33,740
Get him some more.

79
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:35,560
Listen, dear.

80
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,100
I am not long for this world.

81
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:45,220
When I die, you get yourself to the
Joestar mansion along with this letter.

82
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,800
The fool thinks he owes me.

83
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:50,100
This is your ticket to greatness.

84
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,660
It's your only chance, Dio.

85
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:56,728
Go out there and take this
useless world for all you can get.

86
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,240
Crawl on back to your damn manor,
little Lord Fauntleroy. Let's go.

87
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:10,620
You okay?

88
00:05:10,940 --> 00:05:12,140
Just leave me alone!

89
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:13,580
I'll be fine!

90
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:16,057
I did not take a beating
just now for your sake!

91
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:18,316
So whatever you're thinking, stop it!

92
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:21,865
All I want is to conduct
myself as a gentleman.

93
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:24,340
I spotted a damsel in distress.

94
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:26,640
A true gentleman has no fear.

95
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:28,577
He'll fight for those who can't.

96
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:33,013
Even knowing it's a fight he has no
chance of winning, he enters the fray.

97
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:37,254
Someday, I'll have the strength to win.

98
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:44,877
Devil that you were, you drove
mother to an early grave.

99
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:46,195
I'm glad you're dead.

100
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:47,988
May you burn for your sins.

101
00:05:48,460 --> 00:05:52,560
The riches that eluded your grasp,
I will claim them in excess.

102
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:56,777
You lacked the cunning to take
what you wanted, but I'll prevail.

103
00:05:56,860 --> 00:05:58,920
This Joestar shall be the key.

104
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:00,270
Now burn!

105
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:10,420
I will claim what is rightfully mine.

106
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:19,060
Jonathan Joestar.

107
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:24,720
This is the tale of two young men,
their destinies bound to intersect,

108
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:28,340
and the stone mask that
changes their fates forever.

109
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:00,640
Who is he?

110
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:04,280
You must be Dio Brando, right?

111
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:08,160
And you're Jonathan, heir
to the Joestars. Yes.

112
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:09,715
Please, call me Jojo.

113
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:11,587
It's a pleasure to meet you.

114
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:13,850
Danny!

115
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:16,320
That's Danny.

116
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:19,246
He's my dog as well as
my steadfast companion.

117
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,430
Don't worry.

118
00:07:20,513 --> 00:07:22,832
He knows better than to nip at strangers.

119
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,600
What was that for?

120
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:29,720
How dare you!

121
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:33,040
So this is the brat I must usurp.

122
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:35,237
Where's his heart on his sleeve?

123
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:36,700
He's quick to anger.

124
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:40,771
This pampered fool is no match
for the likes of Dio Brando.

125
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:41,980
Fighting already?

126
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,762
I would know what this is about.

127
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:47,590
Sorry.

128
00:07:47,673 --> 00:07:50,580
The dog jumped at me, and
in my haste, I struck it.

129
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:55,940
Welcome to the manor.

130
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:59,780
Consider yourself a part
of the family. Everyone.

131
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:04,757
I would have died in the crash that claimed
my wife were it not for Dio's father.

132
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:07,357
You will treat him as
you would my own son.

133
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:08,960
Very well, your lordship.

134
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:11,140
This is your home now, Dio.

135
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:13,991
Please avail yourself of all its comforts.

136
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:17,640
Thank you, sir, for taking
in this poor unfortunate.

137
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:20,260
Jojo has lost his mother as well.

138
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:22,220
And you're the same age.

139
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:25,000
You'll be thick as thieves soon, Jojo.

140
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:27,180
Dio didn't mean to hurt Dany.

141
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:28,550
Right.

142
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:30,300
It stands to reason, father.

143
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:34,020
If a strange dog jumped at
me, I'd be surprised too.

144
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:40,720
I wish his apology had been more sincere,
but as we'll be living here together,

145
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:43,120
I'll do my utmost to be friendly.

146
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:44,960
This way, Dio.

147
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:46,808
I'll show you your chamber.

148
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:48,230
Yes, sir.

149
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:55,220
You're hurting me!

150
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:56,297
Please let go!

151
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:57,380
Watch your hands.

152
00:08:57,580 --> 00:09:00,397
No one's allowed to touch my
things without my permission.

153
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,310
What?

154
00:09:01,393 --> 00:09:04,780
Next time you reach for what's
mine with this paw, I'll break it.

155
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:07,040
I was only trying to help.

156
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:11,520
I will have a servant
carry them up for me.

157
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:18,840
Listen, I may be a guest within your
house, but I am not to be trifled with.

158
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,820
In all things that I do, I am number one.

159
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:24,717
Look down your nose at
me and you'll regret it.

160
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:27,100
But Dio, I want for us to be friends.

161
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:29,597
And another thing, I hate all mongrels.

162
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:30,980
They don't scare me.

163
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:33,885
I just despise how they
fawn over the unworthy.

164
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:37,889
So keep that mangy mutt of yours
well away from me, Joestar.

165
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:41,300
Dio, what's keeping you? Hurry along.

166
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:42,720
Yes, sir.

167
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:49,580
With Dio's sudden arrival, Jojo's
carefree life spiraled into one of misery.

168
00:09:51,780 --> 00:09:53,980
You got another one wrong, Jojo.

169
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,120
Look at Dio.

170
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:56,260
20 out of 20.

171
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:57,615
Not a single mistake.

172
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:04,820
Jojo, your table manners
are simply abhorrent.

173
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:07,274
You act as if you were raised in a bar.

174
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:10,940
Clear Jojo's plate at once.
He's had enough. What?

175
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:13,057
That's all the dinner you get tonight.

176
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:16,817
It's clear to me that I failed in
your upbringing when I look at Dio.

177
00:10:16,900 --> 00:10:18,841
If your mother could see you now.

178
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:21,260
Dio's manners are impeccable.

179
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:28,920
What an oaf.

180
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:34,280
Our first Fugilist up is Jonathan Joestar.

181
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:38,209
He's been looking
stronger lately, I'd say.

182
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:42,560
As for his opponent today, it's
a boxer we haven't seen before.

183
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:45,497
He's a newcomer to our fair city.

184
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:46,992
All we know is his name.

185
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:48,640
It can't be.

186
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:55,040
Introducing our surprise
opponent, Dio Brando.

187
00:10:56,580 --> 00:11:00,197
Same as ever, land a hit to the other
guy's face and the match is over.

188
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:01,110
Now fight!

189
00:11:09,180 --> 00:11:11,260
Look at him, dojo tits!

190
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:12,877
I've never seen the like!

191
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:14,020
I can't connect!

192
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:17,860
The pampered brat can box,
I'll grant him that much.

193
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:19,890
However...

194
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:26,037
He's never had to punch his way
out of a scrape in the slums,

195
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:28,060
and thus I hold the advantage.

196
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:29,640
Take this!

197
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:31,760
There it is!

198
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:34,020
Jojo loses the fight!

199
00:11:34,380 --> 00:11:36,960
Your suffering isn't over yet, Jojo.

200
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:40,297
I'll jam a thumb into
your eye for good measure,

201
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:42,733
lest you forget who you're dealing with!

202
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:49,720
That arm of his is unreal.

203
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:52,577
Dio, that punch was simply amazing!

204
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:54,760
How did you dodge him so well?

205
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:58,517
It's just a little defensive
footwork I acquired along the way.

206
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:01,957
If you'd like to learn it, I'd be more
than happy to teach it to you fellas!

207
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:03,037
You would do that.

208
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:05,777
Do take care that nobody shows it to Jojo.

209
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:08,137
He can't keep a secret to save his life!

210
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:09,517
You don't say.

211
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,953
Thanks for the warning.

212
00:12:11,580 --> 00:12:13,620
The thumb in my eye.

213
00:12:13,860 --> 00:12:15,340
That was on purpose.

214
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:21,372
Loneliness will devour a man from within.

215
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:24,520
I'll reduce Jojo to an empty husk.

216
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:29,080
Bit by devious bit, I'll steal
the life he was meant to have.

217
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:32,673
By the time we're grown,
there'll be nothing left of him.

218
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:37,760
Damn that Dio.

219
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:39,520
It's terrible.

220
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:42,179
He's ruining everything he touches.

221
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:43,780
Look alive, fellas.

222
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:47,220
Hey, it's me, Jonathan.

223
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:48,678
What are you doing?

224
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:49,918
Mind if I join you?

225
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:51,470
Huh.

226
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:54,844
I could have sworn I heard
a voice a moment ago.

227
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Just a snitch.

228
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:57,395
Better to ignore him.

229
00:12:57,540 --> 00:12:58,580
What did you say?

230
00:12:58,980 --> 00:13:00,260
I'm a snitch, huh?

231
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:03,000
Call me that to my face. Time to go.

232
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:04,637
You're just nothing but a snitch.

233
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:05,897
Do you always write about you?

234
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:08,097
You're just a stupid rich boy, Tattletail.

235
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:10,017
Tell me what I snitched about then!

236
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:11,320
He's lying to you!

237
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:13,716
Why do you just take him at his word?

238
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:15,180
JoJo the Squealer!

239
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:17,730
Dio!

240
00:13:17,813 --> 00:13:18,740
He's slandering me!

241
00:13:19,060 --> 00:13:21,940
He lies and lies and
people just eat it up!

242
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:25,905
From the first day he showed up,
he's been trying to destroy me!

243
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,500
Damn you, Dio Brando!

244
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:32,380
Dio! Dio! Dio! Dio! No!

245
00:13:36,820 --> 00:13:39,920
Ever since he arrived,
everyone's turned on me.

246
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:41,220
Even father.

247
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:44,500
Oh, Danny.

248
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:48,468
I know you will always be my
friend, no matter what Dio does.

249
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:57,750
Huh?

250
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:03,940
Who was that girl just now?

251
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:07,280
I feel as though I have
seen her face before.

252
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:11,380
That's my handkerchief.

253
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:12,960
She brought grapes.

254
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:15,460
Hey, thank you for the fruit.

255
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:19,220
You know, I'll be here tomorrow
if you want to come back.

256
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:23,766
Didn't even tell me her name.

257
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:24,770
Just ran away.

258
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:27,304
Girls are such a curious bunch.

259
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:33,640
A dark time in Jonathan's life was suddenly
made brighter by love's growing embers.

260
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:38,540
The two became fast friends, and
Jonathan was enchanted by her.

261
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:42,100
Iran Pendleton, the name
is music to my ears.

262
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:43,600
She's an angel.

263
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:47,600
What on earth are you
doing to that poor tree?

264
00:14:48,860 --> 00:14:52,360
Jojo, what possessed you
to do that? Goodness.

265
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:57,540
Farewell, Iran. Till next time.

266
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:15,600
Your name wouldn't happen
to be Iran, would it?

267
00:15:15,860 --> 00:15:19,400
You and Jojo, you make such
a smart-looking couple.

268
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:22,575
Really, I should have guessed as much.

269
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:24,760
Try as I might to ruin his life,

270
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:28,116
young Master Jonathan has
been oddly happy as of late.

271
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:35,870
He?

272
00:15:35,953 --> 00:15:36,783
He did it!

273
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:40,220
Give her the what for?

274
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:43,300
The trouble I'd get into
if I was brave as Dio.

275
00:15:43,460 --> 00:15:44,837
He just does what he wants.

276
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:45,802
Devil may care.

277
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:50,200
Tell me, have you and Jojo kissed yet?

278
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:52,220
I'll take that as a no.

279
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:56,740
You thought your first kiss
would be Jojo, but it was I, Dio.

280
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:03,137
Even though it was by force, the
fact that I kissed her is enough.

281
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:05,837
I've killed their romance before it began!

282
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:09,857
I'll deny Jojo the comfort
of friendship and love.

283
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:11,200
What the?

284
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:14,596
Just look at her, Dio She's
taking leave of her senses

285
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:16,497
What's wrong with her?

286
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:18,937
That's disgusting Washing
out her mouth with

287
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:22,100
a muddy puddle Why would anybody do that?

288
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:24,300
There's a stream not far away

289
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:27,180
You ungrateful wench!

290
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:30,595
You dare suggest my kiss is
something to be washed off!

291
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:39,380
Cool your temper, you damnable fool.

292
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:41,895
She's not worth losing your head over.

293
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:44,460
We're done here. Come on.

294
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:50,060
Arena! Hey there!

295
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:57,180
Arena, wait!

296
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,140
Why'd she run off?

297
00:16:59,340 --> 00:17:00,752
Was it something I said?

298
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:04,457
Look at him, fellas.

299
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:06,317
He doesn't know why she ran away.

300
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,697
What do you say we tell him?

301
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:10,797
He deserves to know what his
precious arena's been up to.

302
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:11,710
I don't know.

303
00:17:11,793 --> 00:17:14,878
I'd feel bad making his
little lordship start to cry.

304
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,640
This is his doing.

305
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:20,020
What have you done, Dio?

306
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:22,100
What have you done to my arena?

307
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:25,670
RAAAGH!

308
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:28,910
DIO!

309
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:34,060
Hush, boy!

310
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:38,237
You won't speak my name in vain again
if you know what's good for you.

311
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:39,680
We end this now!

312
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:42,802
I won't let you sully an
innocent maiden's honor!

313
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,940
Your fight is with me, dammit!

314
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:46,720
Upset about Iran?

315
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:48,917
That she shared her favors with me?

316
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,577
And now you intend to give me a
proper thrashing for my impudence?

317
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:55,137
This time, Dio, you have gone too far!

318
00:17:55,220 --> 00:17:58,161
You may be right, but
you're the one who'll pay...

319
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:02,237
Looking to repeat your
performance from our boxing match?

320
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:03,300
Be my guest.

321
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:09,220
I can't beat him.

322
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:15,720
But if I lose here now, I'll spend the
rest of my life cowering in Dio's shadow.

323
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:19,380
Most of all, I have to
fight for Irina's honor.

324
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,000
She needs a champion!

325
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:24,260
Time to end this little pissing match.

326
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:27,000
I'll beat him here, in his own home.

327
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:31,957
Once and for all, he'll know his proper
place in this world is under my heel.

328
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,717
He'll see that it's useless
to try and defeat me.

329
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:37,100
I shall be master, now and always.

330
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:39,800
Come on!

331
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:44,910
Perfect!

332
00:18:44,993 --> 00:18:46,020
Right in the face!

333
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:51,400
How are you able to grab me
after such a blow to the head?

334
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:53,660
Perhaps I was too gentle with you!

335
00:18:58,200 --> 00:18:59,030
Dio!

336
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:01,990
Impossible!

337
00:19:02,073 --> 00:19:05,060
I'm going to beat you till
you cry like a baby, Dio!

338
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:08,500
How could a pampered brat
like him best me in a fight?

339
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:30,457
You how how dare you bastard
how dare you strike me

340
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:36,837
Days crying i'll make you
regret that you Filthy car stop

341
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:42,717
it both of you that is
quite enough father i son i

342
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:45,497
know that boys your age are
prone to fisticuffs however

343
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:48,717
jojo i saw you pummeled
Dio mercilessly after the

344
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:51,117
point at which he had obviously
no chance of winning the

345
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:55,537
fight such is the mark of
a coward no excuses to your

346
00:19:55,620 --> 00:20:00,060
chambers both of you i'll
decide your punishment anon

347
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:11,231
that seems strange wonder what's in there?

348
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:13,977
Ah, well.

349
00:20:14,060 --> 00:20:15,900
Probably some are made for out.

350
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:25,790
What's that?

351
00:20:25,873 --> 00:20:27,819
Something got into the incinerator!

352
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:29,797
Oh, mercy!

353
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:31,680
What if a person's in there?

354
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:35,840
They're burning alive, and it's
all my fault for lighting it!

355
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:42,050
Iran?

356
00:20:43,180 --> 00:20:44,420
Damn you, Dio!

357
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:46,560
I beat you fair and square!

358
00:20:46,820 --> 00:20:50,644
But what does it matter if you've
ruined things for Iran and me?

359
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:56,317
We buried him while you were gone, son.

360
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,871
It was nothing you should have to witness.

361
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:01,857
The constable said it
was probably the work of

362
00:21:01,940 --> 00:21:04,764
a burglar who caught sight
of Dany and panicked.

363
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,540
Dio, he's not here.

364
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:10,446
He hasn't yet returned
from school today, sir.

365
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:15,900
Jojo fled to his room and
fell into a dreamless slumber.

366
00:21:16,660 --> 00:21:19,060
When he awoke, he thought of Danny,

367
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:24,960
his loyal pet and one true
friend, now lost to him, and wept.

368
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:27,510
Yes,

369
00:21:27,593 --> 00:21:29,997
I may have evened the
score by killing his mutt,

370
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:34,277
but it doesn't change the fact that
Jojo is far stronger than I'd thought.

371
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:37,360
Bloody his nose, and he
comes back twice as fierce.

372
00:21:37,740 --> 00:21:39,760
My anger makes me vulnerable.

373
00:21:40,580 --> 00:21:42,180
I must remedy that.

374
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:47,220
Once I learn to master my temper, I'll
be invincible to the likes of Jojo.

375
00:21:48,360 --> 00:21:51,600
In the blink of an eye,
seven years passed.

376
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:07,077
I'll be the roundabout.

377
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:11,257
The words will make you out and out.

378
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:14,560
And spend the day your way.

379
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:19,337
Call it morning, driving through the sun.

380
00:22:19,420 --> 00:22:21,000
And in and out the valley.

381
00:22:31,360 --> 00:22:34,097
The music, dance and sing.

382
00:22:34,180 --> 00:22:38,317
They make the children really ring.

383
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:42,580
I'll spend the day your way.

384
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:46,477
Call it morning, driving through the sun.

385
00:22:46,560 --> 00:22:48,240
And in and out the valley.

386
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:52,920
In and out around the lake.

387
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,337
Miles come out of the sky.

388
00:22:56,420 --> 00:22:58,000
And they'll stand there.

389
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:04,800
One mile over, we'll be
there and we'll see you.

390
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:11,140
Ten and two summers, we'll
be there and laughing too.

391
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:17,057
Twenty-four and five
mile over, we'll see you.

392
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:19,900
I'll be there with you.

393
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:29,957
Seven years later...

394
00:23:30,040 --> 00:23:32,437
The bowl is plucked out
of the air by our hero!

395
00:23:32,520 --> 00:23:34,397
Having read it, all has been made clear.

396
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:36,977
If you're looking to lose
body parts, do stick around.

397
00:23:37,060 --> 00:23:37,997
We are friends no more!

398
00:23:38,080 --> 00:23:39,017
You heard father.

399
00:23:39,100 --> 00:23:40,420
Never again, Dio!
